WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.800
Hi my name is Pedram Mokrian. I'm an Adjunct&nbsp;
Professor here at Stanford School of Engineering.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.680
This course is designed for people that are&nbsp;
looking to get a better perspective on what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:15.120
exactly AI is about and demystify some of these&nbsp;
notions in terms of what is machine learning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.360
how is it different from AI, what are some of&nbsp;
the applications, where is the future going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.680
We're going to begin with taking a historical&nbsp;
view of AI, a very high level view of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.920
technologies, how are we actually applying this AI&nbsp;
infrastructure and advancements in the technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.800
that we're getting into business outcomes. We're&nbsp;
going to try to bring this all together by giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.160
you an idea of how to think more strategically&nbsp;
about how do you actually put in place an AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.880
strategy as part of an existing product or&nbsp;
actually creating an entirely new product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:54.240
line or service line that's centered around AI.&nbsp;
Joining me are going to be a myriad of folks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.160
that are coming from industry themselves with a&nbsp;
depth of background and artificial intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.200
that is world-class. You have large amounts&nbsp;
of data that these machines will be able to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.960
given our guidance, run through very quickly&nbsp;
find the patterns, find the signals, and start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.680
create potentially either better products for you&nbsp;
or new products for you. And that's really what's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:22.240
driving almost all of the the data-driven business&nbsp;
strategies now is is going out and getting data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.520
rather than commodity analytics.&nbsp;
We've built a lot of infrastructure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.200
whether by technology or by policy, in&nbsp;
order to manage just the data aspect of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:39.840
before we even start looking at it from an AI&nbsp;
algorithm what can we learn from a perspective.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.440
So we're really really excited to be able&nbsp;
to share some of these insights with you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:53.040
and we're excited to get this course underway.

